          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>DACDAT</name>
              <description>DAC 12-bit Holding Data\nThese bits are written by user software which specifies 12-bit conversion data for DAC output. The unused bits (DAC1_DAT[3:0] in left-alignment mode and DAC1_DAT[15:12] in right alignment mode) are ignored by DAC controller hardware.\n12 bit left alignment: user has to load data into DAC1_DAT[15:4] bits.\n12 bit right alignment: user has to load data into DAC1_DAT[11:0] bits.</description>
